\citet{RefWorks:297} as indicators of school districts in transition from insular 
to competitive in their politics. In general, the relationship to turnout is 
modest with the strongest relationships being a postive correlation between 
percentage elderly and school board turnout and a negative correlation between 
turnout and population size. 

